{
 "id": "sd-farm-soil-truth",
 "name": "SD: an arable farm and its soil: the truth",
 "description": "Tests an effect closing a balancing loop: soil nitrogen (a stock outside the crop's chain) speeds up crop growth through a diminishing-returns lookup (a table sampled from log(1 + N/40)/log(1 + 200/40): the first kilos of nitrogen matter most). Every tonne harvested into the barn takes 0.35 kg N per hectare out of the soil (a co-flow), so a heavy harvest slows next season's growth; fallow, manure and fertiliser restore nitrogen toward a target. Dry and wet years are not announced; the start of crop rotation (nitrogen restored faster, to a higher level) is.",
